Colossus is a known character in the  Marvel Universe and what makes him  tricky to handle in the CG world is that  he is shiny oh because he's made  completely out of a metallic surface we  also have to do these reflection passes  in the environment whenever we finished  shooting our Colossus motion capture  actor we end up going in and we shoot  clean plates which just allow us to have  all the information that we need for  when Colossus moves around and then we  also shoot reflective gray balls and  reflective silver balls that allows the  visual effects artist to understand  where all the lighting sources are  coming from and then on top of that we  shoot HDR eyes with a still camera and  so we'll go in and they'll set up still  camera and they'll shoot all these  panoramic passes at multiple exposures  and those are to have reflection  information so that when the visual  effects artist put the sort of chrome  body on to Colossus they use that HDRI  information along with their reflection  passes to get sort of all of that  mapping of the environment around him  because he's essentially a giant mirror  that moves around and that allows  Jonathan and our sort of VFX team to  make this seamless transition into this  metallic person that moves like a human  and acts like a human but has this very  otherworldly form
 

